==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|cuneātus}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} [[wedge]]-[[shaped]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} wedge-shaped, with the [[narrow]] part at the [[base]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} having [[straight]], or almost straight sides meeting at the [[apex]] or base.

====Usage notes====
A [[deltoid]] organ is roughly triangular in shape, but may have much less obvious "angles". An [[obdeltoid]] one is practically the same, except that the cuneate leaf's angle are better defined. Being cuneate does not prevent being [[sagittate]].

